Z||000000||Posthumane||07-31-2001||08:11 PM||||After driving around for a while, if I park my car and then try to start it a few minutes later, it won't crank. After letting it sit for about 15 mins, it goes fine again. I thought it might be the neutral safety switch at first, but determined it wasn't because power is definately drained when i try to crank it, it just doesn't turn. The problem caused an embarasing situation for me earlier today, as I was going out to lunch with a hooters girl, and when i went to pick her up, the damn thing wouldn't crank. I had to get a guy to help me push start it. ||||reg||8
