Z||000012||Posthumane||08-08-2001||11:57 PM||||I got the starter problem fixed. I thought it was the solenoid, so i got a new one, and when i went to replace it i found that the battery cable going to it was resting on the muffler, and it had melted through the insulation and causing a short circuit when i tried to crank it. i fixed it by simply taping up the wire and taping it to the frame so it wouldn't touch the exhaust.<P>As for the OTHER update, yes I am now going out with the hooters girl mentioned earlier. BTW, i work at hooters too, as a cook, so if anyone here in calgary wants some wings come on down. I'll try to come down to see you guys at willy's tommorrow after work.||||reg||1
